# Home Assistant Community Add-on: Jackett

Jackett works as a proxy server: it translates queries from applications into tracker-specific HTTP queries, parses the results, and exposes them through a unified API.

## Configuration

The add-on exposes Jackett on port `9117`.

Configuration and Jackett data are stored in `/config` and are mapped to the Home Assistant add-on configuration directory.

## Support

For issues specific to this add-on, use the GitHub repository issue tracker.
